    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0396" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3233</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ewing</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-08T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 5, 6 p.m. I am pleased with the sympathetic attitude of Honduras
                    and the other Central American governments, but the Government of the United
                    States is not in a position to guarantee protection in case of aggression
                    resulting from the proposed action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
